# 0005. One config for macOS and Arch, guarded per OS and per tool

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

## Context
The same shell runs on a Mac (BSD userland) and an Arch desktop (GNU, Wayland or X11), and not
every tool is installed on both.

## Decision
No per-OS branches or files. Differences are handled inline: `(( IS_MAC ))` / `$OSTYPE`, then
`$WAYLAND_DISPLAY`, then X11. Every alias and helper is guarded on its tool
(`(( $+commands[x] ))`) and works when it is missing. Commands use flags both BSD and GNU accept.

## Alternatives
- Separate mac/linux files or branches: drift between them, every change made twice.

## Consequences
- One place to change; a fresh machine with few tools still starts cleanly.
- Every helper needs a guard, and BSD/GNU differences (`sed -i.bak`) need care.

## References
`conf.d/00-env.zsh`, `conf.d/50-aliases.zsh`, CLAUDE.md rules.
